
==============================================================================
E13 -- Trust ablation under heterogeneous priors
==============================================================================
Setup: 30% of agents start with P(paradigm 0) = 0.95 (WRONG);
       70% start with P(paradigm 1) = 0.95 (RIGHT). Truth = paradigm 1.
       Cont substrate, lambda=1.0 (no tempering), q_reliability=0.75.
       Compare trust_learning=False vs trust_learning=True.

condition              mean_qB_final   wrong_bloc_final   right_bloc_final
  trust_learning=False            0.995              0.993              0.996
  trust_learning=True             0.995              0.993              0.996

Trust marginal on WRONG-bloc convergence: +0.000
  Positive = trust learning prevents wrong-bloc convergence (lock-in).

